# What never needs uploading to a builder.
#
# `vercel deploy` from a working copy uploads the directory, and two of the things in a
# developed clone are enormous: `.next` (a local build, ~1 GB with the Turbopack dev cache) and
# `.pglite` (the seeded local database, ~60 MB). Neither is an input to a Vercel build — the
# builder runs `npm run build` itself, and a hosted deployment reads `DATABASE_URL` rather than
# the local WASM database — so uploading them costs minutes and buys nothing.
#
# `.pglite` additionally must not travel: it is a real database containing seeded member rows,
# password hashes and email addresses. A local fixture is still a file full of credentials.

.next/
.pglite/
node_modules/

# Local secrets. Already git-ignored; ignored here too, because a CLI deploy reads the working
# copy rather than the commit, so a `.gitignore` entry is not a guarantee at this boundary.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local

# Not inputs to a build.
docs/
tests/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
